<title>JAPAN: Japan July aluminium imports rise 17.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan July aluminium imports rise 17.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined aluminium imports in July were 252,259 tonnes, up 17.6 percent from 214,431 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry statistics released on Wednesday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (on a customs-cleared basis,</p>
<p>in tonnes):</p>
<p>		  July 96	   June 96     July 95</p>
<p> Total	  252,259	   262,167     214,431</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Brazil	  18,060	    38,398	26,692</p>
<p> Russia	  46,000	    40,939	34,974</p>
<p> Australia     30,510	    52,757	25,764</p>
<p> U.S.	    41,453	    27,610	16,402</p>
<p>Refined aluminium imports in the first seven months of 1996 were 1,575,819 tonnes, off 8.9 percent from 1,730,144 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
